WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.890
In 1791, the United States added the
First Amendment to its Constitution.

2
00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:11.750
It begins: Congress shall make no law
respecting an establishment of religion.

3
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:17.740
A few years earlier, in 1787, British
campaigners made a medallion that asked:

4
00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:20.390
Am I not a man and a brother?

5
00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:24.480
So after 1750, did religion prop up power,

6
00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:26.620
or help people challenge it?

7
00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:29.470
In this mission, you'll
meet prophets and rebels,

8
00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:32.730
from southern Africa to the
plains of North America.

9
00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:37.400
Then you'll test the evidence for a
bold claim about religion and power.

10
00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:42.210
Your mission: find out whether religion
propped up power or helped people challenge

11
00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:44.120
it, after 1750.
